  "imagery": "Photography is used for emotional impact only — the hero features a dramatic close-up of a screaming man against pure black, no lifestyle context, no product integration. The image IS the message: browsers are frustrating, Dia is the catharsis. Product screenshots appear as floating browser-window mockups with traffic-light dots, tab bars, and full URL bars, treated as objects displayed on the page rather than embedded UI. The screenshots use real content (mountain landscape for 'Friday Brief', slide decks for 'Decks') to demonstrate Dia's output quality. No illustrations, no abstract graphics, no 3D renders. Icon style: minimal outlined icons, thin stroke weight, monochrome black or white. Imagery density is sparse — the page is text-dominant with one hero photograph and 3-4 product mockup windows, everything else is typography and white space.",
